<title>GERMANY: Hanover Re says not affected by Paris train blast.</title>
<headline>Hanover Re says not affected by Paris train blast.</headline>
<dateline>HANOVER, Germany 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>German reinsurer Hannover Rueckversicherungs AG said on Thursday it would not be affected by Tuesday's bomb in a Paris rush-hour train by suspected Algerian Islamic guerrillas which killed two people.</p>
<p>The German reinsurance group, which is active in France, said French rail company SNCF was not privately insured because of its massive size.</p>
<p>Injuries to individuals would be covered by a state fund administered by government authorities and not affect French direct insurers nor their reinsurers, said Hannover Re, one of the world's largest reinsurance groups.</p>
<p>Hannover Re said it expected &quot;positive returns&quot; from the French market in 1996 despite fire damage last month in the Eurotunnel and a major fire in May at the Paris headquarters of French bank Credit Lyonnais.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
